built in IOC container. Before I show you&nbsp;
what advantages dependency injection brings,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:50.480 --> 00:10:56.640
let's see a scenario where there is no&nbsp;
dependency injection. In a typical application,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:56.640 --> 00:11:03.360
let's say we have three pages right now. And we&nbsp;
have some common functionality that we want to use&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:03.360 --> 00:11:10.960
across all the three pages. Like let's say we want&nbsp;
to send emails, and we want to access our database&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:10.960 --> 00:11:16.560
in all the three pages that we have. Now,&nbsp;
let's imagine that on these three pages,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:16.560 --> 00:11:22.400
we need to access the database first. So&nbsp;
what we will do is we will create the object&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:22.400 --> 00:11:28.400
for database classes on all the three pages, we&nbsp;
will have to open that connection, we will have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:28.400 --> 00:11:34.000
to do the database operation. And then we will&nbsp;
have to close the connection in all the places&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:34.960 --> 00:11:40.800
to do the same and create object for email&nbsp;
implementation that we have in all the three&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:40.800 --> 00:11:48.160
pages. So you can see this is a lot of duplicate&nbsp;
code. On top of that, what happens in future,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:48.160 --> 00:11:52.960
if you change the implementation of&nbsp;
how you access the database, or email,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:53.760 --> 00:11:59.440
based on the current configuration, you might have&nbsp;
to make that change in all of the three pages,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:00.080 --> 00:12:06.880
which is a big mess, because right now it's three&nbsp;
pages down the line, it could be 30, or 300 pages.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:07.920 --> 00:12:13.520
Another issue here is that on each page,&nbsp;
you will deal with creating the object,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:13.520 --> 00:12:20.160
managing them as well as disposing them. And&nbsp;
that will be a time consuming effort when we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:20.160 --> 00:12:26.720
have to do that in all the pages. So that&nbsp;
being said, what is the solution to avoid&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:26.720 --> 00:12:33.520
all of this and get an optimal architecture. The&nbsp;
answer to all of that is dependency injection.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:34.560 --> 00:12:40.560
First, let me show how this scenario would look&nbsp;
like. Again, we will have the three pages. And we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:40.560 --> 00:12:47.280
will have email and database functionality. These&nbsp;
are the common things that we had before as well.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:47.920 --> 00:12:54.240
But now we will have something special, which&nbsp;
is dependency injection container. So as you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:54.240 --> 00:13:01.600
can see, we have got our dependency injection&nbsp;
container that will have an ID email and an IDE&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:01.600 --> 00:13:09.040
interface and its implementation. So inside our&nbsp;
container, we have the implementation of the eye&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:09.040 --> 00:13:16.880
email interface and the IDB interface. When any&nbsp;
page will need access to these functionalities, it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:16.880 --> 00:13:23.360
will just ask the dependency injection container&nbsp;
to create an object of this functionality and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:23.360 --> 00:13:31.200
directly give page an object to use. So inside&nbsp;
the page, we will actually be using an interface.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:31.200 --> 00:13:39.200
And then dependency injection does audits magic of&nbsp;
passing the object when the website needs it, that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:39.200 --> 00:13:46.000
we do not have to deal with creating the object&nbsp;
disposing or managing that object inside our pages&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:47.200 --> 00:13:54.160
or pages will look very clean with just the&nbsp;
interface all the instance and implementation will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:54.160 --> 00:14:01.280
be done by dependency injection container. Now in&nbsp;
future if you want to change or replace the email&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:01.280 --> 00:14:07.920
class, you do not have to make any changes in&nbsp;
the pages, all you have to do is just change the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:07.920 --> 00:14:14.560
implementation inside the email class. And since&nbsp;
we are registering that in the container, next&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:14.560 --> 00:14:21.440
time when we build the project, it will take the&nbsp;
new implementation. So you can see we only have to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:21.440 --> 00:14:27.840
change in one place. Now. That is one of the main&nbsp;
advantage that comes with dependency injection.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:28.720 --> 00:14:34.880
Now in order to use dependency injection, you&nbsp;
can use many third party tools. But with dotnet&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:34.880 --> 00:14:40.880
core we have a built in dependency injection&nbsp;
container and that has its own advantages.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:42.000 --> 00:14:47.680
So I hope that you have a short overview&nbsp;
of how Dependency injection is helpful.&nbsp;&nbsp;

